hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3070","###
 Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansur, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: ""Urwa bin Az-Zubayr and I entered the mosque, and there we found Abdullah bin Umar sitting beside the chamber of Aisha (RA). We saw the people in the mosque performing the Duha prayer. So we asked him about their prayer, and he said: 'It is an innovation (Bid'ah).' Then he asked: 'How many Umrahs did the Messenger"
"3071","**
Narrated to us Bundār, narrated to us Abū Dāwūd, narrated to us Hammām, from Qatādah who said:
I asked Anas ibn Mālik (RA): ""How many 'Umrahs did the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) perform?""
He (RA) replied: ""Four 'Umrahs. And he performed one Hajj. And his 'Umrah was combined with his Hajj."""
